WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.260
Here's a city, shaded from its least
deprived neighbourhoods to its most deprived.

2
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:10.180
Psychosis, like schizophrenia, turns out
to be more common in the most deprived

3
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.280
neighbourhoods.

4
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:15.970
And it's more common among adults
out of work than among those in work.

5
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.050
So which way round is it?

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.860
Does poverty lead to illness?

7
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.310
Or does illness lead to poverty?

8
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.150
In this mission, you'll see why a
link like this is a correlation,

9
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.410
and why that alone can't
show which causes which.

10
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.540
Then you'll weigh up two explanations
that point in opposite directions,

11
00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.990
and test examples against each one.

12
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.830
Your mission: decide which comes
first, the poverty or the illness.
